  "assets": "assets/scenes/slingshot_domino",
  "implementation_policy": "CPU solve (physics/physics.py through physics/simulate_cli.py): PyBullet rigid 6-DOF bodies (plastic ball 1.85 g, r = 7.5 mm; wooden domino 12 x 35 x 75 mm, 16 g; light rigid leather pouch) and two extensible neo-Hookean flat rubber bands (40 segments, 9 cm x 4 mm x 0.18 mm, E = 1 MPa, Kelvin viscosity, weak strip bending) with finite-width contact against the exact Y-frame profile, 4800 substeps per frame (19200 for heavy_ball); release at 0.5 s, 4 s recorded at 24 Hz (frame k = t (k-1)/24 s) plus a separate 72 Hz slow series. The timed edit heavy_domino_at_frame_12 changes the domino mass and inertia x10 with PyBullet changeDynamics at t = 11/24 s inside the running solve, so frames 1-11 equal the source. appearance/render_scene.py replays the native states in Blender 4.3.2 (Cycles, CUDA); the published look adds appearance/realism_overlay.py through one audited hook. --stage verify checks the accepted native delivery (renders/slingshot_domino/delivery/accepted) and the published timed edit. Materials are plausible SI values, not calibrated on a real specimen.",
